  "summary": "I'm a Senior Java Backend Developer with 10+ years of enterprise experience and 8+ years of deep specialization in Pharmacy Benefit Management — all at Express Scripts / Cigna, the nation's largest PBM.  \n\nFor the past 8+ years I've been the main senior backend owner of APW-BES, the core microservice powering the MAP Prescriber Portal. That means 200+ RESTful and GraphQL API endpoints serving 1.4+ million physicians across prior authorization (ePA), prescription workflows, patient registration, clinical decision support, and secure document intake — all HIPAA-compliant, all at enterprise scale.  \n\nWhat I bring that's hard to find elsewhere: \n→ Deep PBM domain expertise: ePA, formulary, prescriber portals, 2PC drug scheduling, delegate management \n→ Enterprise Java leadership: Spring Boot, Java 17+, Kafka, Okta/OAuth2, SAML SSO, OpenShift, Oracle \n→ Production ownership: I've diagnosed and resolved critical async defects and registration failures in a system serving over a million physicians — with no escalation path and no backup \n→ AI-augmented development: I use Cursor IDE and Claude daily to accelerate delivery on complex PBM feature work  \n\n📩 Always interested in connecting with engineering leaders and innovators in the PBM and healthcare IT space.",
