    "description": "Sole senior Java backend owner of APW-BES — core PBM microservice powering the MAP Prescriber Portal for 1.4M+ physicians across ePA, Rx workflows, registration, and clinical decision support.\n\nDesigned and maintained 200+ RESTful and GraphQL API endpoints — one of the largest API surfaces in the Express Scripts PBM ecosystem — supporting HIPAA-compliant transactions at enterprise scale.\n\nEngineered core PBM workflows: Two-Point Contact (2PC) drug scheduling, future-drug automation, bulk registration, delegate management, and secure document intake pipelines.\n\nImplemented enterprise identity & authorization via Okta (MFA, user lifecycle), OAuth2/JWT, LDAP, and Spring Security — meeting HIPAA and CMS requirements across all API surfaces.\n\nLed SAML-based SSO integration connecting Ann & Robert H. Lurie Children's Hospital of Chicago to the MAP Prescriber Portal — enabling secure, federated identity access for hospital physicians into the PBM platform.\n\nDiagnosed and resolved critical production defects including async failures in document upload and a NonUniqueResultException in prescriber registration — zero escalation, zero downtime.\n\nDeployed and operated on OpenShift; managed routes, pods, and scaling for high-availability PBM production environments.\n\nLeveraged AI coding tools (Cursor, Claude) daily to accelerate Spring Boot development and optimization on complex PBM feature work.",
